#
# SGLang v0.5.19 + our SM121 build patches. Created 2026-09-10 to track the
# v0.5.19 line (released 2026-09-03/05, 786 PRs / 214 contributors). NOT BUILT
# YET: no acceptance-gate run, no GPU/serving run. Treat everything here as
# first-contact until scripts/verify_sglang_image.sh has passed on the image.
#
# THE HEADLINE: this is the QUIETEST bump of the line on the BUILD side and the
# LOUDEST on the RUNTIME side.
#   1. Build side: nothing moved. The sgl-kernel tree stays at
#      python/sglang/kernels/aot/ (package "sglang-kernel", still 0.4.6.post1),
#      torch stays at 2.13.0 (so BASE_IMAGE is unchanged and no new base build
#      is needed), transformers / kernels / cutlass-dsl pins are all unchanged.
#      The one CMakeLists change is cosmetic in intent and fatal in practice:
#      the C++ standard became a cached variable, so every literal "-std=c++17"
#      turned into "-std=c++${SGL_KERNEL_CXX_STANDARD}" and that line is the
#      trailing context of arch-prune hunk 1 -> new SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT.
#   2. flashinfer 0.6.18 is now REQUIRED, not merely pinned: the release's own
#      Breaking Changes say --dsa-topk-backend flashinfer and the CuTe-DSL NVFP4
#      W4A16 mode have NO fallback for pre-0.6.18 APIs (#36954, #33237, #35120).
#      This is the first recipe in the line where staying on the previous
#      flashinfer is not a valid rollback.
#   3. Runtime side: v0.5.19 rewrote server_args.py (-6.5k lines) and
#      overrides.py (-1.9k), i.e. the two biggest runtime-patch targets we have.
#      The runtime patch set in roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/ has NOT been
#      replayed against this ref yet. See OPEN RISK A; that replay is the gate
#      on promoting this recipe, not an afterthought.
#
# ── DELTA vs sglang-0.5.18-sm121.recipe ─────────────────────────────────────
#   1. SGLANG_VERSION 0.5.18 to 0.5.19, SGLANG_REF to v0.5.19.
#   2. SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT "-v0.5.18" to "-v0.5.19". NOT cosmetic:
#      `set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)` became
#      `set(SGL_KERNEL_CXX_STANDARD "17" CACHE STRING ...)` +
#      `set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD ${SGL_KERNEL_CXX_STANDARD})`, and the three nvcc
#      flag lists now say "-std=c++${SGL_KERNEL_CXX_STANDARD}". Hunk 1 of
#      sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.18.patch has that literal as context and FAILS
#      on this ref, which would abort the build in the container dry-run. The
#      pruned RESULT is unchanged. All four -v0.5.19 files regenerated with zero
#      fuzz and zero offset, see PATCH VERIFY.
#   3. FLASHINFER_VERSION 0.6.17 to 0.6.18.post1 (see the block below and
#      point 2 of the headline). Upstream pins ==0.6.18; .post1 is that plus one
#      additive cherry-pick and is the newest STABLE, which is the pin policy
#      this line has always followed (0.6.15.post1, 0.6.16.post3 before it).
#   4. APPLY_NEMOTRON35_SPEC_PR36186 1 -> 0. The flag's documented expiry has
#      arrived: v0.5.19 CONTAINS 41e7612dee (#36186 plus its two DFlash2
#      prerequisites #35371/#35496), verified with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`.
#      Re-applying it would fail the in-container dry-run. Consequence for the
#      better: the Nemotron-3.5-Lightning MTP / DFlash / DSpark drafts are NATIVE
#      on this image, no backport involved.
#   5. APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497 1 -> 0, and this one is a CAPABILITY LOSS, see
#      OPEN RISK F. PR #36497 is still unmerged (no qwen4_exp anywhere in
#      v0.5.19), but sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch is a diff of the upstream
#      branch rebased onto v0.5.18 and it does NOT apply to v0.5.19: 15 files
#      with rejected hunks (server_args.py, arg_groups/overrides.py, environ.py,
#      unquant.py, hybrid_linear_attn_backend.py, forward_batch_info.py, ...).
#      So this image does NOT serve RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4.
#   6. BASE_IMAGE / TRANSFORMERS / KERNELS / CUTLASS_DSL / HF_HUB / AUDIO /
#      ACCELERATE / SGL_KERNEL_DIR / TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT: ALL UNCHANGED.
#      v0.5.19 still pins torch==2.13.0, transformers==5.12.1,
#      kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15 and nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2.
#   7. Upstream dependency churn that rides along with the ref (informational,
#      none of it a knob here): sgl-deep-ep 0.1.0 -> 0.1.2, sgl-deep-gemm
#      0.1.5.post3 -> 0.1.7, tilelang 0.1.11 -> 0.1.12, compressed-tensors now
#      PINNED (==0.18.0, was unpinned), NEW tokenizers==0.22.2 (0.23.0rc0 breaks
#      transformers' CLIPTokenizer), mooncake 0.3.13. sglang-kernel stays
#      0.4.6.post1, quack-kernels 0.6.4, cuda-tile 1.6.0rc5 and apache-tvm-ffi
#      0.1.11 unchanged. [build-system] requires gained torch==2.13.0 and
#      setuptools-rust>=1.11; both are INERT here, the Dockerfile installs the python
#      package with `uv pip install --no-build-isolation --no-deps ./python`, so
#      the build backend never resolves that list.
#
# ── PATCH VERIFY (2026-09-10, host-side, against raw v0.5.19 source) ─────────
#   OK sgl-kernel-arch-prune-v0.5.19.patch        REGENERATED (hunk 1 context)
#   OK sgl-kernel-disable-fa3-v0.5.19.patch       regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-sm90-target-v0.5.19.patch  regenerated, content identical
#   OK sgl-kernel-skip-flashmla-v0.5.19.patch     regenerated, content identical
#      Produced the same way as the -v0.5.18 set: apply in build order, fix the
#      one drifted hunk by hand, re-diff each step, so all four land with ZERO
#      fuzz and ZERO offset and the four "dgxarley ..." marker pairs (8 total)
#      are present afterwards. Re-applying the whole set to pristine v0.5.19
#      reproduces the reference tree byte for byte. Cross-checked BOTH ways: the
#      -v0.5.18 files FAIL on v0.5.19 and the -v0.5.19 files FAIL on v0.5.18
#      (arch-prune hunk 1 in both directions), so a recipe that forgets to move
#      the suffix aborts loudly instead of building unpatched.
#   OK sglang-dsv4-mtp-marlin-v0.5.14.patch       applies (offset 217); still
#      NEEDED: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method in v0.5.19 still goes
#      straight to Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod with no marlin branch.
#   OK sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch  clean (path
#      python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py unchanged).
#      Kept ON even though upstream moved its tilelang pin 0.1.11 -> 0.1.12; the
#      uint8-view arg check is what the hunk works around and the hunk still
#      lands, so dropping it is a separate, testable decision.
#   NO sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch       MERGED into this ref, GATED OFF
#      (all 5 hunks of dflash.py reject, as expected for merged code).
#   NO sglang-qwen4exp-pr36497.patch              DOES NOT APPLY, GATED OFF
#      (15 files with rejects). See DELTA 5 / OPEN RISK F.
#   NO sgl-kernel-sm121.patch                     target still gone, GATED OFF
#      (unchanged since v0.5.16, PR #30448: no nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh, no
#      cutlass_moe_fp4 in v0.5.19 either).
#   -- Dockerfile chain NOT re-verified for this ref yet (scitrera origin/main is
#      unchanged at 2a3b1b7 and the chain was clean on v0.5.18; the patches are
#      against the Dockerfile, not against sglang, so drift is unlikely, but it
#      is a dry-run away and the build does it anyway).
#
# ── OPEN RISKS, validate before this recipe is promoted ──────────────────────
#   A. RUNTIME patches (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_patches/): REPLAYED and then
#      RE-ANCHORED 2026-09-11 on spark5. Offline replay is now 0 ANCHOR-DRIFT on
#      v0.5.19 AND on the v0.5.18 control, in all three gate scenarios, and
#      idempotent on both. Harness, logs and patched trees: /root/patchreplay-0519
#      on spark5 (re-run: `SRC=dist-src TAG=0519 ./replay2.sh`).
#      Harness: fake dist-packages = v0.5.19 python/sglang + this recipe's source
#      patches (marlin, tilelang), plus the REAL dependency packages the recipe
#      pins (flashinfer 0.6.18.post1, transformers 5.12.1, cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 via
#      flashinfer's bundled CuTeDSL copy) instead of stubs, so p29 / p56 / p60 get
#      real signal. Three gate scenarios (bare, GLM-5.2, Hy3, the latter two with
#      SGLANG_SPECULATIVE_ENABLED=true), each replayed twice for idempotency, plus
#      a CONTROL replay against v0.5.18 + all four of that recipe's source patches
#      + flashinfer 0.6.17, i.e. the image deployed today. The control is what
#      makes each finding attributable to the ref rather than to the harness, and
#      what proves the re-anchors did not regress instances pinned to the older
#      image: every fix below is a replace_any spelling or an alt_target, never a
#      rewrite of the old anchor.
#      WHAT DRIFTED AND WHAT WAS DONE (12 edits over 6 patches):
#        p30 - DSA torch indexer backend, 3 edits, all now two-spelling:
#              (a) is_sm100_supported() -> get_platform().is_sm100 (v0.5.19's new
#              srt/runtime_context platform object); (b) the module-level
#              *_CHOICES constants are gone, the lists are inline in the
#              Arg(choices=[...]) declaration; (c) DSATopKBackend(server_args.
#              dsa_topk_backend) -> DSATopKBackend.resolve(model_runner) (#36313).
#              The injected mirror-resolve also follows the ref: it reads
#              get_exec().kernel.<arg> on v0.5.19, matching what the Indexer does
#              there, since the whole point of that line is to agree with it.
#        p34 - kv_cache_configurator.py: server_args.<arg> -> get_exec().kernel.
#              <arg> (#35907). Third replace_any spelling.
#        p37 - THE load-bearing one (NVFP4-KV + speculation), 3 edits:
#              the forward_extend KV read was rebuilt around use_fmha_v2 +
#              _reshape_paged_kv_cache(); the fixed-q-len verify call moved into
#              the helper _run_fixed_q_len_decode(), which forwards kv_cache_sf
#              but takes no mask and splits the batch by KV length, so the
#              FP4 + q_len>1 path now calls the kernel directly (as before) while
#              every other path keeps the helper WITH kv_cache_sf passed through;
#              and the flashinfer draft-extend-v2 metadata call gained a trailing
#              kv_view kwarg. Two things worth knowing beyond the anchors:
#              the injected FP4 branch must still define is_decode_mode (the rest
#              of forward_extend reads it), and v0.5.19's NEW ragged verify layout
#              (spec_info.ragged_verify_layout) calls the kernel without block
#              scales or mask. Correctness there under FP4 is UNVERIFIED, so the
#              patch REFUSES that combination with an actionable RuntimeError
#              rather than risking the silent word salad it exists to prevent.
#              If a future profile wants nvfp4 KV + a ragged-verify spec algo,
#              that is the thing to work out, not a flag to flip.
#        p44 - NOT re-anchored: v0.5.19's qwen3_5_mtp.load_weights applies
#              QWEN3_5_KV_SCALE_MAPPER itself, so the patch got the same
#              target_contains self-gate p51 has and now logs "gate not matched".
#        p59 - overrides.py was split into arg_groups/model_overrides/<model>.py
#              (the @_register_for dispatch went from 28 uses to 1) with
#              overrides.py left as a re-export shim. Sub-patch (1) now targets
#              model_overrides/nemotron_h.py FIRST with overrides.py as an
#              alt_target, and its body-header edit got a second spelling
#              (model_config_of(server_args)). Sub-patches (2)/(3) unchanged.
#        p41 - PRE-EXISTING, not caused by this ref: it drifted on the v0.5.18
#              control too, because upstream PR #30331 landed the final_layernorm
#              -> shared_head.norm remap in v0.5.18. Same treatment as p44: a
#              target_contains self-gate. It had gone unnoticed because the
#              v0.5.18 cycle's Hy3 scenario did not also set
#              SGLANG_SPECULATIVE_ENABLED=true, so the patch was never evaluated.
#      After the fixes the ONLY behavioural differences between the two refs are
#      the three intended ones: p44 and p65 gate off on v0.5.19 (upstream absorbed
#      / no qwen4exp source patch) and p59 patches nemotron_h.py instead of
#      overrides.py. Everything else applies identically on both.
#      CLEAN on v0.5.19 without any work, worth recording because three of them
#      patch dependencies rather than sglang: p43 and p57 (re-anchored last cycle)
#      still apply, p29 patches flashinfer's bundled CuTeDSL mma.py, p56 applies
#      against transformers 5.12.1, p60 against flashinfer 0.6.18.post1's
#      jit/cpp_ext.py. p36 self-gates off (upstream passes uniform_q_len itself).
#      What the replay still canNOT answer, and only the acceptance gate on the
#      built image can: whether the modules p30/p35 GENERATE actually import (the
#      2026-07-28 p30 fp8_kernel incident: patch reports success, module is
#      unimportable, 31 model classes silently drop out of the registry). The
#      harness reduces write_module's import probe to a syntax check.
#      One open question for the gate rather than the replay: p29's first path
#      nvidia_cutlass_dsl/python_packages/cutlass/... does not exist in the 4.6.2
#      wheels (they ship nvidia_cutlass_dsl/dsl_packages/ with MLIR bindings
#      only), so only the flashinfer-bundled copy was patched here. Check on the
#      built image whether its own cutlass-dsl install still has a second copy
#      under a path p29 knows.
#   B. INHERITED from v0.5.16, still open: moe_runner_backend cutlass / triton
#      for NVFP4 is gone (#30448), so nvidia/Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-NVFP4 (cutlass)
#      and Minimax-M2.5 @ PP=4 (triton) still need re-testing or re-pinning, and
#      compressed-tensors NVFP4 MoE with apply_router_weight_on_input=True still
#      asserts instead of running. See TURBOQUANT.md.
#   C. NEW in v0.5.19, from the release's own "Breaking Changes":
#      * The unified radix tree is now the default cache for EVERY model, not
#        just hybrid ones (#35081). SGLANG_ENABLE_UNIFIED_RADIX_TREE is
#        deprecated. Every profile on this image is on a new cache path.
#      * DeepSeek-V4 FP4 EXPERT checkpoints default to the FlashInfer MXFP4 MoE
#        runner on SM90/SM100/SM120 when --moe-runner-backend is auto (#35919).
#        Our profiles pin flashinfer_cutlass explicitly, and an explicit backend
#        is preserved, so this should not move us; verify on the DSV4 profiles.
#      * W4A4 MegaMoE moved to --enable-w4a4-megamoe; the two
#        SGLANG_OPT_DEEPGEMM_MEGA_MOE_* env vars now only warn (#35918).
#      * Constructing a ServerArgs no longer resolves it (#35907), see RISK A.
#      * Requests are capped at 32 stop strings / 32 stop regexes of <= 256
#        bytes each, HTTP 400 beyond that (#37029).
#      * Spark3 was renamed Spark2.5 (model_type spark2_5, tool-call parser
#        "spark" -> "spark25") (#36416), irrelevant here, no such profile.
#      Carried over from v0.5.18 and still true: the DSV4 fused MHC post+pre path
#      and MoE deferred finalize are ON BY DEFAULT (escape hatches
#      SGLANG_ENABLE_MOE_DEFERRED_FINALIZE=False,
#      SGLANG_OPT_UNIFIED_CACHE_FREE_OUT_OF_WINDOW_SLOTS=False), torchao is gone,
#      and the SM120 FP8 per-tensor GEMM backend is cuBLAS.
#   D. TORCH: no gap. v0.5.19 still pins torch==2.13.0, which is exactly what
#      BASE_IMAGE ships (xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132, built
#      2026-08-28). No new base build for this recipe.
#   E. INHERITED dependency shapes the missing_deps step will try to install:
#      cuda-tile==1.6.0rc5 still has no PyPI wheel for that version (wheel-stub
#      sdist redirecting to pypi.nvidia.com; fix is --extra-index-url
#      https://pypi.nvidia.com, not unpinning). sgl-deep-ep moved 0.1.0 -> 0.1.2
#      and sgl-deep-gemm 0.1.5.post3 -> 0.1.7: re-check both ship cp312 aarch64
#      wheels before the build, they are new versions of packages that only
#      became wheels last cycle. missing_deps.py only checks PRESENCE, not
#      version, so anything already installed stays at the installed version.
#   F. QWEN3.8-FLASH-NEXT IS NOT ON THIS IMAGE. APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=0 (the
#      v0.5.18-based branch diff does not rebase onto v0.5.19 by patch(1)), so
#      qwen4_exp / Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration does not exist here and
#      RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 fails at load with "has no SGLang
#      implementation". The profile
#      roles/k8s_dgx/model_profiles/radixark-qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4.yml PINS
#      xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.18-sm121 explicitly, so it keeps working on
#      the old image and nothing regresses by promoting this one, but do not
#      point that profile here.
#      To bring the model forward: the upstream branch qwen4-main-squashed has
#      MOVED ON (head 4ccff141 of 2026-09-07, 11 commits over merge-base
#      861eca8e, including three GB10-relevant ones: 78c5024e9d "restore SM121
#      correctness", 3a09f089e0 file-backed PLE table for unified-memory devices
#      / DGX Spark, 9b2aee2283 loading nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4, plus
#      c8457de59a for a GB10 NEXTN collapse). Re-capturing means rebasing those
#      11 commits onto v0.5.19 (17 conflicted files / ~48 conflict hunks on the
#      first commit alone) and re-cutting the squashed diff: a separate piece
#      of work with SM121 correctness implications, not a version bump. Until
#      then p65 (the runtime half: GB10 decode repair + trtllm-gen SM121 veto)
#      simply self-gates off here.
#   G. INHERITED: NVFP4 ATTENTION on SM121 (flashinfer #3897) is still only
#      KERNEL-level verified (2026-07-28 on spark5), never validated end to end
#      through SGLang with a real uniform-NVFP4 model. Judge output quality by
#      pattern-grep plus token distribution plus tail, not by finish_reason.
#      flashinfer moves two minor releases here (0.6.17 -> 0.6.18.post1), so
#      re-run those checks rather than carrying verdicts.
#   H. SM12x work in v0.5.19 we have NOT exercised (check for redundancy BEFORE
#      re-porting runtime anchors, same lesson as the v0.5.16
#      fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch_sm120 absorption): #35116 SM120 flash_mla
#      page-split buffer allocation, #35739 NVFP4 diffusion on sm_120, the DSA
#      prefill top-k v2 kernel (#35175) and --speculative-dsa-topk-backend
#      (#36313) which sit right on top of what p30/p34/p35 do by hand, and the
#      MiniMax-H3 / Ling-3.0-flash / Qwen3.8-27B DGX Spark cookbook entries.
#
# ── DEPLOY NOTE: SGLANG_CACHE_DIR (#32434, since v0.5.18) ───────────────────
# Triton, FlashInfer, Inductor, DeepGEMM and the CUDA driver cache all live
# under SGLANG_CACHE_DIR, so the FIRST launch on this image recompiles once.
# Setting any of TRITON_CACHE_DIR / FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE /
# SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR / TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR / CUDA_CACHE_PATH keeps that one
# where it is. We already set FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE explicitly in
# roles/k8s_dgx/tasks/sglang_instance.yml, so the expensive flashinfer JIT cache
# is NOT affected; the DeepGEMM cache is, and is the other expensive one.
#
# Prerequisite: xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132 present on the
# build host (scripts/build_pytorch_base_image.sh, see ensure_base_image_present
# in build_sm121_image.sh). UNCHANGED from v0.5.18; it is already there if that
# image was built.
#
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
TARGET=runtime

# UNCHANGED from the v0.5.18 recipe: v0.5.19 still pins torch==2.13.0
# (torchvision 0.28.0, torchaudio 2.11.0, triton 3.7.1), so the 2.13.0-v1-cu132
# base built 2026-08-28 still matches upstream exactly. Do NOT rebuild the base
# for this recipe.
BASE_IMAGE=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev:2.13.0-v1-cu132

# flashinfer 0.6.18.post1 (2026-09-05). BUMPED from 0.6.17, and this bump is
# MANDATORY, not opportunistic: v0.5.19's Breaking Changes list flashinfer 0.6.18
# as REQUIRED: #36954 moved the pin, and #33237 / #35120 removed the fallbacks
# for pre-0.6.18 APIs behind --dsa-topk-backend flashinfer and the CuTe-DSL
# NVFP4 W4A16 mode. Rolling back to 0.6.17 is therefore NOT a valid escape from
# a 0.5.19 problem; roll the whole recipe back to 0.5.18-sm121 instead.
#
# Why .post1 and not the bare 0.6.18 upstream pins: .post1 is 0.6.18 plus
# exactly one additive cherry-pick (#4931, an OPTION to skip checking active
# rows in TRTLLM ragged prefill) and a version bump, and "newest STABLE" is the
# pin policy this line has followed throughout (0.6.15.post1, 0.6.16.post3).
# If a 0.6.18-only regression is ever suspected, `FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18` is
# a one-line, same-ABI step down.
#
# SM12x content in 0.6.18 (2026-08-29) worth knowing about: MXFP4 MoE coverage
# extended to Blackwell RTX PRO *and DGX Spark*, SM107/Rubin completion (not
# ours, but it is what most of the release is), trtllm-gen FMHA reshuffling.
# The 0.6.17 rationale still applies underneath: #3932 (b12x FP4 quantization
# numerics fix, the reason W4A4 output quality has to be re-measured rather
# than carried over), #4253, #4130, #4117, #3903, #4161, #4380, #4101, plus the
# older #3897 / #3838 / #3960 / #3922.
#
# Wheels verified 2026-09-10 on https://flashinfer.ai/whl, all three packages
# exist at 0.6.18.post1 including the one that matters for arm64:
#   flashinfer-python    0.6.18.post1  (py3-none-any)
#   flashinfer-cubin     0.6.18.post1  (py3-none-any)   <- not on PyPI, only here
#   flashinfer-jit-cache 0.6.18.post1+cu130 manylinux_2_28_aarch64
# FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18
FLASHINFER_VERSION=0.6.18.post1

# transformers 5.12.1 - exactly v0.5.19's pyproject pin (==5.12.1, unchanged
# since v0.5.15). Do NOT bump past the SGLang ref (no perf benefit, transformers
# is not in the inference hot path).
TRANSFORMERS_VERSION=5.12.1

# kernels 0.14.1 - exactly v0.5.19's constraint (kernels>=0.14.1,<0.15,
# unchanged). PERF-NEUTRAL on SM121: the only hub-loaded kernel
# (sgl-flash-attn3) is hard-disabled on GB10 and has no sm_121/ARM64 builds.
KERNELS_VERSION=0.14.1

# nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2 - UNCHANGED, still exactly v0.5.19's pyproject pin
# (nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.6.2). The explicit pin stays mandatory because
# NVIDIA has shipped different wheel CONTENT under the same version number
# before (the 4.5.2 mlir_global_dtors 'data' ICE, see
# reference_cutlass_dsl_wheel_swap).
# Re-verify on the built image with the rmsnorm smoke test from the v0.5.18
# recipe (and confirm the DSL path is actually TAKEN: norm/__init__.py falls
# back to CUDA JIT SILENTLY when the DSL cannot target the arch).
# Fallback: 4.6.1, then 4.6.0.
CUTLASS_DSL_VERSION=4.6.2

# Audio multimodal deps - see the 0.5.15.post1 recipe. SGLang pulls numba itself;
# librosa is still needed (soundfile/audioread).
AUDIO_DEPS="librosa"

# accelerate - baked into the image (ModelOptModelLoader imports it).
ACCELERATE_DEPS="accelerate"

# huggingface_hub FLOOR (not an exact pin), unchanged. Guards against the xet
# gated-repo download bug (hub PR #4394 forwarded the REDACTED xetHash for GATED
# repos to hf_xet -> "Unable to parse string as hex hash value"); fixed by hub
# PR #4595 in v1.26.0. See FIXED_UPSTREAM_HF_XET_BUG.md. Installed as the LAST
# pip action of the builder stage so nothing can downgrade it afterwards.
HF_HUB_MIN_VERSION=1.26.0

SGLANG_VERSION=0.5.19
SGLANG_REF="v0.5.19"

# main-ahead sgl-kernel patch variant. Kept at 1 for provenance (the -v0.5.19
# files carry the mainahead content, the mscclpp link refactor is still in the
# tree), but SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT takes precedence in apply_patches(), so
# the -mainahead siblings themselves are not used on this ref.
SGL_KERNEL_MAINAHEAD=1

# Suffix of the four CMakeLists source patches to install under the canonical
# names. "-v0.5.19" = the -v0.5.18 edits regenerated against v0.5.19, where
# arch-prune hunk 1 additionally had to be re-cut because upstream replaced the
# literal "-std=c++17" with "-std=c++${SGL_KERNEL_CXX_STANDARD}". All four
# regenerated with zero fuzz and zero offset. Empty/absent in pre-0.5.17 recipes.
SGL_KERNEL_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.19"

# Where the sgl-kernel tree lives inside the sglang checkout (moved there by RFC
# #29630 in v0.5.17), passed to the Dockerfile as ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default
# "sgl-kernel", so older recipes are byte-identical). UNCHANGED in v0.5.19; MUST
# match the path in the patch variant above.
SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot

# ── CORE SM121 JIT-header patch: TARGET STILL GONE (PR #30448) -> OFF ────────
# python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh has not returned in
# v0.5.19 (verified 2026-09-10) and cutlass_moe_fp4() is still absent; NVFP4 MoE
# runs through FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, the backend our model
# profiles pin anyway (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass). At 1 the
# in-container dry-run would abort the build. Consequence: see OPEN RISK B.
APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 FlashMLA kernel: DROPPED (native since v0.5.13) ──────────────
FLASH_MLA_REPO=
FLASH_MLA_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_REPO=
DSV4_KERNEL_REF=
DSV4_KERNEL_ARCH=

# ── DeepSeek-V4 NVFP4 MoE: NATIVE since v0.5.14 (PR #25820) -> OFF ──────────
APPLY_DSV4_NVFP4_PR25820=0

# ── DeepSeek-V4 EAGLE-MTP marlin branch + TileLang indexer compat -> ON ──────
# Unchanged rationale: HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method still has no marlin
# branch for the MTP/nextn draft-MoE layers in v0.5.19 (it goes straight to
# Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod, verified 2026-09-10), and the TileLang uint8
# arg check still bites. Both source patches dry-run-verified against v0.5.19
# on 2026-09-10 (marlin: offset 217; tilelang: clean).
APPLY_DSV4_MTP_MARLIN_TILELANG=1

# Variant of the tilelang compat patch. "-v0.5.16" selects
# sglang-tilelang-018-indexer-compat-v0.5.16.patch: the path introduced by RFC
# #29630 (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/) and only the uint8-view hunk,
# because upstream adopted the 2D alloc_shared half. That file name is a
# GENERATION label, not a ref restriction; the path and the hunk are unchanged
# in v0.5.19, verified clean, even though upstream's own tilelang pin moved to
# 0.1.12.
TILELANG_PATCH_VARIANT="-v0.5.16"

# ── Qwen3.6 ModelOpt mixed NVFP4: MERGED (PR #27906) -> OFF ─────────────────
# The OPEN dispatch fix #28099 is a RUNTIME patch in sglang_launch.sh and is
# unaffected by this flag (p21/p22); re-check Qwen3.6 live.
APPLY_QWEN36_MIXED_NVFP4_PR27906=0

# ── Qwen4-Exp / Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: STILL OPEN UPSTREAM, PATCH STALE -> OFF ──
# PR #36497 has NOT merged (no qwen4_exp in v0.5.19), but the patch on disk is a
# squash of the upstream branch qwen4-main-squashed @ 99c9362e diffed against a
# v0.5.18-era base, and it does NOT apply to v0.5.19: 15 files with rejected
# hunks. Turning it on would abort the build in the in-container dry-run.
# CONSEQUENCE: this image refuses RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 at load
# ("has no SGLang implementation"). That model's profile pins the older
# 0.5.18-sm121 tag explicitly, so it keeps working there. Re-enabling means
# re-capturing the patch from the (advanced) upstream branch rebased onto
# v0.5.19; see OPEN RISK F for the commit list and conflict scope.
APPLY_QWEN4EXP_PR36497=0

# -- Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding: NATIVE since this ref -> OFF -
# The documented expiry of this flag has arrived. v0.5.19 CONTAINS 41e7612dee,
# i.e. PR #36186 ("[Model] Support Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding")
# together with its two DFlash2 prerequisites #35371 and #35496 (verified with
# `git merge-base --is-ancestor 41e7612dee v0.5.19`). Re-applying merged code
# fails the in-container dry-run and aborts the build.
# The MTP / DFlash / DSpark drafts for
# nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4 are therefore NATIVE on this
# image. The profile
# roles/k8s_dgx/model_profiles/nvidia-nvidia-nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b-nvfp4.yml
# still pins 0.5.18-sm121 (where they came from the backport); moving it here is
# a deliberate, separate change.
APPLY_NEMOTRON35_SPEC_PR36186=0

IMAGE_TAG=xomoxcc/dgx-spark-sglang:0.5.19-sm121
